<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_secrets_connector" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Zeebe Modeler" exporterVersion="0.8.0">
  <bpmn:process id="connectorSecretResolution" name="Connector secret resolution benchmark" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Drives the outbound-connector secret-resolution code path with real process
instance throughput, instead of hitting the /v2/secrets/resolve and /v2/secrets/list REST
endpoints directly. Each instance activates one io.camunda:http-json:1 job whose "headers"
input is built from batchSize placeholders, each a {{secrets.&lt;keyPrefix&gt;&lt;index&gt;}}
reference; the connector runtime resolves every one of them through CentralStoreSecretProvider
(legacy FALLBACK mode) before issuing the HTTP call, so the benchmark measures the same gateway
resolve-secrets call the standalone driver used to exercise, but through the code path a real
customer (e.g. Connectors-triggered secret resolution) actually uses.

The header index for placeholder i is modulo(businessKey + modulo(i, uniquePerBatch), poolSize),
where businessKey is the Starter's per-instance monotonic counter (see StarterProperties):
- batchSize placeholders per job exercise the connector's secret cache within a single job
  execution, measuring the effect of resolving the same handful of names repeatedly in one
  request (batch-dedup): set uniquePerBatch &lt; batchSize so some indices repeat.
- poolSize controls how many distinct secrets exist across the whole run. A small poolSize (e.g.
  1) keeps every job cache-first after warm-up; a poolSize approaching or exceeding the cache's
  effective capacity forces store-miss traffic, since businessKey increments every instance and
  poolSize rotates through that many distinct names before repeating. poolSize secrets must be
  seeded (secretsConnectorBenchmark.count in the load-test-setup chart) to match.
- keyPrefix must match the seeded Secret's key prefix (secretsConnectorBenchmark.keyPrefix).

batchSize, uniquePerBatch, poolSize and keyPrefix are process variables set by the Starter's
payloadPath (see load-tests/docs/secrets-connector-benchmark.md for the default and preset
payload files). businessKey is set automatically per instance by the Starter.

The task calls the connectors pod's own actuator health endpoint rather than an external
service: the goal is to measure secret-resolution overhead added to a job activation, not to
benchmark an arbitrary downstream HTTP target, and this avoids depending on external network
access from the load-test cluster.

The unused "_secretAllowlistSeed" input exists only to make every BENCHMARK_TOKEN0..4999 name
appear literally in this element's zeebe:input text. Under SECRET_FILTER_MODE=STRICT (required
whenever LEGACY_MODE=FALLBACK, see camunda-platform-values-secrets-connector.yaml), the
connector runtime derives its per-element secret allow-list by statically regex-scanning every
zeebe:input source string for the deployed model — it never evaluates the FEEL expression, so a
name computed only at runtime (as the "headers" input's index is) would never appear in that
scan and would be silently filtered out. The seed input's value is never read or used for
anything; its only purpose is to be scanned. It covers indices up to the largest poolSize any
preset payload uses (5000, the store-miss preset) so every preset's real, dynamically-selected
name is already on the allow-list.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="start" name="start">
      <bpmn:outgoing>toResolveSecret</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="resolveSecret" name="Call http-json with secret header">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="get" target="method" />
          <zeebe:input source="http://connectors:8080/actuator/health" target="url" />
          <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=context merge(for i in 0..(batchSize - 1) return context put({}, &#34;X-Secret-&#34; + string(i), &#34;{{secrets.&#34; + keyPrefix + string(modulo(businessKey + modulo(i, uniquePerBatch), poolSize)) + &#34;}}&#34;))" target="headers" />
          <zeebe:input source="10" target="connectionTimeoutInSeconds" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN0}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN1}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN2}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN3}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN4}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN5}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN6}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN7}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN8}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN9}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN10}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN11}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN12}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN13}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN14}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN15}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN16}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN17}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN18}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN19}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN20}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN21}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN22}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN23}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN24}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN25}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN26}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN27}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN28}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN29}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN30}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN31}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN32}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN33}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN34}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN35}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN36}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN37}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN38}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN39}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN40}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN41}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN42}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN43}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN44}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN45}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN46}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN47}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN48}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN49}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN50}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN51}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN52}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN53}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN54}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN55}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN56}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN57}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN58}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN59}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN60}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN61}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN62}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN63}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN64}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN65}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN66}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN67}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN68}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN69}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN70}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN71}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN72}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN73}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN74}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN75}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN76}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN77}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN78}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN79}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN80}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN81}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN82}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN83}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN84}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN85}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN86}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN87}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN88}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN89}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN90}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN91}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN92}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN93}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN94}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN95}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN96}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN97}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN98}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN99}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN100}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN101}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN102}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN103}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN104}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN105}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN106}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN107}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN108}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN109}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN110}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN111}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN112}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN113}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN114}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN115}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN116}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN117}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN118}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN119}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN120}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN121}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN122}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN123}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN124}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN125}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN126}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN127}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN128}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN129}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN130}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN131}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN132}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN133}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOKEN134}}{{secrets.BENCHMARK_TOK